# Ignore rules for `docker build -f apps/web/Dockerfile .`
#
# The name matters. Docker reads `.dockerignore` from the root of the build
# context, and this image is built from the monorepo root — so a file at
# apps/web/.dockerignore would be silently ignored. BuildKit (default since
# Docker 23, and what Coolify uses) looks for `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore`
# first, which is what lets each app have its own list.

# --- never ------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.github
**/node_modules
**/.turbo
**/.next
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. The image takes NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL as a build arg and nothing
# else; a stray .env in the context is a secret one COPY away from being baked
# into a layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# --- not part of this image -------------------------------------------------
# The Tauri app. src-tauri/target alone is gigabytes of Rust build output, and
# none of it is reachable from the site.
apps/desktop
# The API. Its own image builds from apps/server/Dockerfile.
apps/server
# No database dependency here — see the Dockerfile's package list.
packages/db

# The design archive: ~100 PNGs and four multi-hundred-kilobyte HTML sheets.
# The sprite engine is vendored into packages/ui, so nothing at build time
# reads this.
designs
docs
scripts

# --- noise ------------------------------------------------------------------
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/coverage
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
README.md
AGENTS.md
docker-compose.yml
biome.json
bts.jsonc
